<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <RootNamespace>KendoNET.DynamicLinq</RootNamespace>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <PropertyGroup>
    <PackageId>KendoNET.DynamicLinq</PackageId>
    <Title>KendoNET.DynamicLinq</Title>
    <Authors>CoCo Lin</Authors>
    <Description>Implements server paging, filtering, sorting, grouping and aggregating for Kendo UI via Dynamic Linq, targeting .NET 10.</Description>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
1. Breaking: An eq filter on a date column matches the exact instant instead of expanding into the whole of that calendar day. Filter with a gte/lt range instead, as the README shows.
2. DateTime filter values are read as instants in UTC instead of being converted to the server's time zone, so results no longer depend on where the application runs.
3. Date filter values are now coerced for DateTime?, DateTimeOffset and DateTimeOffset? columns, which previously received no date handling at all.

Full changelog: https://github.com/linmasaki/KendoNET.DynamicLinq/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md
    </PackageReleaseNotes>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/linmasaki/KendoNET.DynamicLinq</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/linmasaki/KendoNET.DynamicLinq</RepositoryUrl>
    <PackageIconUrl>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/linmasaki/CoCoPackageIcon/master/cocodotnet64.png</PackageIconUrl>
    <PackageIcon>Icon.png</PackageIcon>
    <PackageTags>net dotnet kendo kendo-ui linq dynamic-linq</PackageTags>
    <PackageVersion>10.1.0</PackageVersion>
    <Version>10.1.0</Version>
    <Copyright>Copyright © 2017-2026 CoCo Lin</Copyright>
    <PackageLicenseFile>LICENSE</PackageLicenseFile>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="System.Linq.Dynamic.Core" Version="1.7.3"/>
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\LICENSE" Pack="true" PackagePath=""/>
    <None Include="..\Icon.png" Pack="true" PackagePath=""/>
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
